# Submissions & Disputes (QA workflow)

The workflow that consumes a scored audit form: an audit is assigned, drafted,
submitted, scored, optionally disputed, and finalized (with unlock/reopen for
corrections). Scoring math itself lives in
[.cursor/rules/forms-scoring.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/forms-scoring.mdc); this rule
covers everything downstream. Follows
[.cursor/rules/backend-api-conventions.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/backend-api-conventions.mdc).

## Statuses

- Submission (`models/Submission.ts`): `DRAFT → SUBMITTED → DISPUTED? → FINALIZED`.
- Dispute (`types/dispute.types.ts`): `OPEN → UPHELD | REJECTED | ADJUSTED`.
  Never mutate these ad hoc; score changes from a dispute go through
  `utils/disputeScoreHistory.ts`.

## Backend map (`backend/src/`)

- `services/SubmissionService.ts` — assignment, draft/submit, scoring, flagging
  (wired inline from `routes/submission.routes.ts`).
- `services/qa/` — completed-list, detail, export, `qa.submissions.finalize.service.ts`,
  `qa.submissions.notify.ts`, `qa.dashboard.service.ts` (barrel `index.ts`).
- Disputes: `controllers/dispute.controller.ts` (CSR create/read/update/history),
  `controllers/manager/disputes.controller.ts` + `services/manager/manager.disputes.*`
  (manager list/detail/resolve/export), `routes/dispute.routes.ts`.
- Unlock/reopen: `services/unlock/*` + `controllers/unlock.controller.ts` +
  `middleware/disputeUpload.ts`.
- QA controllers: `controllers/qa/submissions.controller.ts`,
  `controllers/trainer/submissions.controller.ts` (read path).

## Frontend map (`frontend/src/pages/quality/`)

`SubmissionDetailPage.tsx` composes `submission-detail/*` panels (`ScorePanel`,
`ReviewDetailsPanel`, `CallDetailsPanel`, `DisputePanel`/`DisputeForms`,
`UnlockBanner`/`UnlockDialog`/`ReopenedNotice`). Lists: `SubmissionsPage.tsx`,
`DisputesPage.tsx`. APIs: `services/submissionService.ts`, `qaService.ts`,
`unlockService.ts`.

## Query keys

Detail keys are role-scoped (`['submissions','detail',id,roleId]`); follow
[.cursor/rules/query-keys.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/query-keys.mdc) — never drop the
trailing `roleId` when invalidating. Obey [.cursor/rules/ui-design.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/ui-design.mdc).
